<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Russo-Swedish War (1590–1595)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1590">1590</a>–<a href="/years/1595">1595</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Russo-Swedish War of 1590–1595 was fought between the Tsardom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> under Feodor I, guided by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boris-godunov">Boris Godunov</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>. Russia sought to recover the towns on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-finland">Gulf of Finland</a> lost in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonian-war">Livonian War</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-teusina">Treaty of Teusina</a> of 1595 returned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivangorod">Ivangorod</a>, Yam, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/koporye">Koporye</a> and Korela to Russia, while Sweden kept <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonia">Estonia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/narva">Narva</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/russo-swedish-war-1590-1595.jpg" alt="Russo-Swedish War (1590–1595)" width="200" height="250" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Boris_Godunov_(Pushkinsky_zapovednik).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
